    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field for owners so the application satisfies the spec: initials are the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus an `initials(Owner)` default method that computes `\"X.Y.\"` from the first characters of the first and last names (following the existing `displayName` pattern).\n\nTest results:\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` (asserts `$.initials` == `\"J.S.\"` for firstName `john`/lastName `smith`) passes.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures/errors.",
